  h1#header Aldi Pramudya
  p.st AI, Data Science, SWE, anything but #[a(href="https://www.w3schools.com/whatis/whatis_frontenddev.asp") #[span.wr doing frontend]].
  p.summary Semester 7 Computer Science student at #[a(href="https://ipb.ac.id" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") IPB University] (#[span.hl GPA 3.69/4.00], a number I'm legally required to mention). I build and deploy end-to-end ML systems, from data preprocessing and model benchmarking through to API development and cloud deployment. #[span.hl BNSP-Certified Data Analyst], graduate of the #[a(href="https://www.dbs.com/foundation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") DBS Foundation] × #[a(href="https://www.dicoding.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Dicoding] AI Engineering Cohort, and the person behind MoodSense, a mental health monitoring app that reads your mood better than most people do.
  p.summary I led backend development for #[a(href="https://ittoday.web.id/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") IT-Today 2025] (#[span.hl 2,000+ users], none of whom ever saw my CSS) and design clean-architecture APIs with #[a(href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") FastAPI] and #[a(href="https://expressjs.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Express.js]. Comfortable across the stack, from training neural networks in #[a(href="https://www.tensorflow.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") TensorFlow]/#[a(href="https://pytorch.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") PyTorch] to deploying containerized services on #[a(href="https://railway.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Railway] and #[a(href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Vercel]. And no, the frontend joke above was not a lie. #[span.invisible-text I use LaTex for most of my college assignments. It is way better than MSWord or Google Docs. Also you're not supposed to be able to read this part.]
  blockquote
    span Good design is as little design as possible.
    author Some German guy

  h2#projects Projects?
  h3.project-heading
    | Website for IT-Today 2025
    span.project-date January 2025 – November 2025
  p.project-meta IT-Today 2025
  ul
    li Led a team of 10 developers across backend, frontend, and UI/UX divisions.
    li Built 20+ RESTful API endpoints using Express.js, Prisma ORM, and MySQL, with Cloudflare R2 for object storage.
    li Deployed and maintained the API on a cloud platform, serving 2,000+ users during the event.
    li Conducted code reviews and provided technical support to frontend (React) and UI/UX teams.
    li Gathered and modeled requirements through cross-division collaboration with Executive and Competition committees.
    li This project is still maintained, #[a(href="https://github.com/pusdatin-ittoday/ittod-web-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") click here to access github page].

  h3.project-heading
    | Benchmarking Machine Learning Models for SME Success Prediction
    span.project-date May 2026 – June 2026
  p.project-meta INFEST Data Science Competition 2026 (Finalist)
  ul
    li Developed an end-to-end machine learning pipeline to predict SME success using a limited and imbalanced dataset.
    li Benchmarked Logistic Regression, SVM, Random Forest, XGBoost, Gaussian Process Classifier, and Stacking Ensemble.
    li Implemented feature selection (Lasso), class imbalance handling (SMOTE, class weighting, undersampling), and robust evaluation using Nested Cross-Validation and permutation testing.
    li Identified Logistic Regression with Lasso Screening as the most robust model based on MCC and multi-metric evaluation.
    li #[a(href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WfvWF3xqLjho3MLbcnwu13Pvby_XCNju/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access paper].

  h3.project-heading
    | Schola Backend
    span.project-date May 2026 – June 2026
  p.project-meta Academic Project
  ul
    li Architected a Clean Architecture backend with 9 vertical feature slices (auth, submissions, verification, notifications, dashboard, etc.) using FastAPI and async SQLAlchemy.
    li Designed a verifier approval pipeline with sequential/parallel workflows and HMAC-SHA256 e-signature generation for official document signing.
    li Implemented role-based access control with 4 user roles (Mahasiswa, Dosen, Pejabat, Operator), JWT authentication, and rate limiting.
    li Built a dynamic form template system with JSON Schema-based field definitions, supporting multiple letter types (SKA, SKPI, etc.) with auto-generated submission IDs.
    li Integrated Cloudflare R2 for file storage, SMTP-based email notifications, and Docker containerization with auto-seeding demo data on first boot.
    li #[a(href="https://github.com/walidan-nadilaw/Schola/tree/main/backend" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access github page].

